    "segments": [
      {
        "start": 0,
        "duration": 4.116,
        "time": "0:00",
        "text": "Hey everyone, welcome back to Bright Circuits."
      },
      {
        "start": 4.2,
        "duration": 4.116,
        "time": "0:04",
        "text": "Today we're answering a question I get"
      },
      {
        "start": 8.4,
        "duration": 4.116,
        "time": "0:08",
        "text": "all the time: how does a flat"
      },
      {
        "start": 12.6,
        "duration": 4.116,
        "time": "0:12",
        "text": "piece of glass on a roof turn"
      },
      {
        "start": 16.8,
        "duration": 4.116,
        "time": "0:16",
        "text": "sunlight into electricity you can actually use?"
      },
      {
        "start": 21,
        "duration": 4.116,
        "time": "0:21",
        "text": "By the end of this video you'll"
      },
      {
        "start": 25.2,
        "duration": 4.116,
        "time": "0:25",
        "text": "understand the physics inside a solar cell,"
      },
      {
        "start": 29.4,
        "duration": 4.116,
        "time": "0:29",
        "text": "why panels are wired the way they"
      },
      {
        "start": 33.6,
        "duration": 4.116,
        "time": "0:33",
        "text": "are, and what the inverter and battery"
      },
      {
        "start": 37.8,
        "duration": 4.116,
        "time": "0:37",
        "text": "are really doing."
      },
      {
        "start": 42,
        "duration": 4.965,
        "time": "0:42",
        "text": "Let's start with sunlight itself. Light arrives"
      },
      {
        "start": 47.067,
        "duration": 4.965,
        "time": "0:47",
        "text": "in tiny packets of energy called photons,"
      },
      {
        "start": 52.133,
        "duration": 4.965,
        "time": "0:52",
        "text": "and each photon carries an amount of"
      },
      {
        "start": 57.2,
        "duration": 4.965,
        "time": "0:57",
        "text": "energy that depends on its color. Blue"
      },
      {
        "start": 62.267,
        "duration": 4.965,
        "time": "1:02",
        "text": "photons carry more energy than red photons,"
      },
      {
        "start": 67.333,
        "duration": 4.965,
        "time": "1:07",
        "text": "and infrared photons carry less still. On"
      },
      {
        "start": 72.4,
        "duration": 4.965,
        "time": "1:12",
        "text": "a clear day at noon, roughly one"
      },
      {
        "start": 77.467,
        "duration": 4.965,
        "time": "1:17",
        "text": "thousand watts of sunlight land on every"
      },
      {
        "start": 82.533,
        "duration": 4.965,
        "time": "1:22",
        "text": "square meter of ground. That number, one"
      },
      {
        "start": 87.6,
        "duration": 4.965,
        "time": "1:27",
        "text": "kilowatt per square meter, is the standard"
      },
      {
        "start": 92.667,
        "duration": 4.965,
        "time": "1:32",
        "text": "test condition every solar panel is rated"
      },
      {
        "start": 97.733,
        "duration": 4.965,
        "time": "1:37",
        "text": "against. The whole job of a solar"
      },
      {
        "start": 102.8,
        "duration": 4.965,
        "time": "1:42",
        "text": "panel is to catch as many of"
      },
      {
        "start": 107.867,
        "duration": 4.965,
        "time": "1:47",
        "text": "those photons as possible and turn their"
      },
      {
        "start": 112.933,
        "duration": 4.965,
        "time": "1:52",
        "text": "energy into moving electrons."
      },
      {
        "start": 118,
        "duration": 3.702,
        "time": "1:58",
        "text": "So what happens inside a silicon solar"
      },
      {
        "start": 121.778,
        "duration": 3.702,
        "time": "2:01",
        "text": "cell? A solar cell is a thin"
      },
      {
        "start": 125.556,
        "duration": 3.702,
        "time": "2:05",
        "text": "wafer of silicon that has been doped"
      },
      {
        "start": 129.333,
        "duration": 3.702,
        "time": "2:09",
        "text": "with small amounts of other elements. The"
      },
      {
        "start": 133.111,
        "duration": 3.702,
        "time": "2:13",
        "text": "top layer is doped with phosphorus, which"
      },
      {
        "start": 136.889,
        "duration": 3.702,
        "time": "2:16",
        "text": "gives it extra electrons, and the bottom"
      },
      {
        "start": 140.667,
        "duration": 3.702,
        "time": "2:20",
        "text": "layer is doped with boron, which leaves"
      },
      {
        "start": 144.444,
        "duration": 3.702,
        "time": "2:24",
        "text": "gaps called holes. Where those two layers"
      },
      {
        "start": 148.222,
        "duration": 3.702,
        "time": "2:28",
        "text": "meet, you get a p-n junction with"
      },
      {
        "start": 152,
        "duration": 3.702,
        "time": "2:32",
        "text": "a built-in electric field. When a photon"
      },
      {
        "start": 155.778,
        "duration": 3.702,
        "time": "2:35",
        "text": "with enough energy hits the silicon, it"
      },
      {
        "start": 159.556,
        "duration": 3.702,
        "time": "2:39",
        "text": "knocks an electron loose and leaves a"
      },
      {
        "start": 163.333,
        "duration": 3.702,
        "time": "2:43",
        "text": "hole behind. The electric field at the"
      },
      {
        "start": 167.111,
        "duration": 3.702,
        "time": "2:47",
        "text": "junction pushes the electron one way and"
      },
      {
        "start": 170.889,
        "duration": 3.702,
        "time": "2:50",
        "text": "the hole the other way, and that"
      },
      {
        "start": 174.667,
        "duration": 3.702,
        "time": "2:54",
        "text": "separation is what creates a voltage. Connect"
      },
      {
        "start": 178.444,
        "duration": 3.702,
        "time": "2:58",
        "text": "a wire from the front contacts to"
      },
      {
        "start": 182.222,
        "duration": 3.702,
        "time": "3:02",
        "text": "the back contacts and the electrons flow"
      },
      {
        "start": 186,
        "duration": 3.702,
        "time": "3:06",
        "text": "through it as direct current. A single"
      },
      {
        "start": 189.778,
        "duration": 3.702,
        "time": "3:09",
        "text": "silicon cell only produces about half a"
      },
      {
        "start": 193.556,
        "duration": 3.702,
        "time": "3:13",
        "text": "volt, no matter how big it is."
      },
      {
        "start": 197.333,
        "duration": 3.702,
        "time": "3:17",
        "text": "Photons with too little energy pass straight"
      },
      {
        "start": 201.111,
        "duration": 3.702,
        "time": "3:21",
        "text": "through, and the extra energy of blue"
      },
      {
        "start": 204.889,
        "duration": 3.702,
        "time": "3:24",
        "text": "photons is lost as heat, which is"
      },
      {
        "start": 208.667,
        "duration": 3.702,
        "time": "3:28",
        "text": "why the best commercial cells convert only"
      },
      {
        "start": 212.444,
        "duration": 3.702,
        "time": "3:32",
        "text": "about twenty two percent of sunlight into"
      },
      {
        "start": 216.222,
        "duration": 3.702,
        "time": "3:36",
        "text": "electricity."
      },
      {
        "start": 220,
        "duration": 4.628,
        "time": "3:40",
        "text": "Half a volt is not very useful"
      },
      {
        "start": 224.722,
        "duration": 4.628,
        "time": "3:44",
        "text": "on its own, so cells are combined"
      },
      {
        "start": 229.444,
        "duration": 4.628,
        "time": "3:49",
        "text": "into panels. A typical residential panel has"
      },
      {
        "start": 234.167,
        "duration": 4.628,
        "time": "3:54",
        "text": "sixty or seventy two cells wired in"
      },
      {
        "start": 238.889,
        "duration": 4.628,
        "time": "3:58",
        "text": "series, which adds their voltages together to"
      },
      {
        "start": 243.611,
        "duration": 4.628,
        "time": "4:03",
        "text": "roughly thirty to forty volts. The cells"
      },
      {
        "start": 248.333,
        "duration": 4.628,
        "time": "4:08",
        "text": "are sandwiched between tempered glass on the"
      },
      {
        "start": 253.056,
        "duration": 4.628,
        "time": "4:13",
        "text": "front and a polymer backsheet, then framed"
      },
      {
        "start": 257.778,
        "duration": 4.628,
        "time": "4:17",
        "text": "in aluminum to survive decades of weather."
      },
      {
        "start": 262.5,
        "duration": 4.628,
        "time": "4:22",
        "text": "Because the cells are in series, shading"
      },
      {
        "start": 267.222,
        "duration": 4.628,
        "time": "4:27",
        "text": "a single cell can drag down the"
      },
      {
        "start": 271.944,
        "duration": 4.628,
        "time": "4:31",
        "text": "whole string, a bit like a kink"
      },
      {
        "start": 276.667,
        "duration": 4.628,
        "time": "4:36",
        "text": "in a garden hose. That's why modern"
      },
      {
        "start": 281.389,
        "duration": 4.628,
        "time": "4:41",
        "text": "panels include bypass diodes that let current"
      },
      {
        "start": 286.111,
        "duration": 4.628,
        "time": "4:46",
        "text": "route around a shaded group of cells."
      },
      {
        "start": 290.833,
        "duration": 4.628,
        "time": "4:50",
        "text": "Panels are then wired together into strings"
      },
      {
        "start": 295.556,
        "duration": 4.628,
        "time": "4:55",
        "text": "on the roof to reach the voltage"
      },
      {
        "start": 300.278,
        "duration": 4.628,
        "time": "5:00",
        "text": "the inverter expects."
      },
      {
        "start": 305,
        "duration": 4.389,
        "time": "5:05",
        "text": "Now for the part most people skip:"
      },
      {
        "start": 309.478,
        "duration": 4.389,
        "time": "5:09",
        "text": "the inverter. Solar panels produce direct current,"
      },
      {
        "start": 313.957,
        "duration": 4.389,
        "time": "5:13",
        "text": "but your home and the electrical grid"
      },
      {
        "start": 318.435,
        "duration": 4.389,
        "time": "5:18",
        "text": "run on alternating current. The inverter converts"
      },
      {
        "start": 322.913,
        "duration": 4.389,
        "time": "5:22",
        "text": "direct current into alternating current that matches"
      },
      {
        "start": 327.391,
        "duration": 4.389,
        "time": "5:27",
        "text": "the grid's voltage and frequency exactly. Good"
      },
      {
        "start": 331.87,
        "duration": 4.389,
        "time": "5:31",
        "text": "inverters also run maximum power point tracking,"
      },
      {
        "start": 336.348,
        "duration": 4.389,
        "time": "5:36",
        "text": "constantly adjusting the electrical load so the"
      },
      {
        "start": 340.826,
        "duration": 4.389,
        "time": "5:40",
        "text": "panels operate at their most efficient voltage"
      },
      {
        "start": 345.304,
        "duration": 4.389,
        "time": "5:45",
        "text": "as clouds pass and temperature changes. There"
      },
      {
        "start": 349.783,
        "duration": 4.389,
        "time": "5:49",
        "text": "are three main options: a single string"
      },
      {
        "start": 354.261,
        "duration": 4.389,
        "time": "5:54",
        "text": "inverter, microinverters on every panel, or power"
      },
      {
        "start": 358.739,
        "duration": 4.389,
        "time": "5:58",
        "text": "optimizers paired with a central inverter. Microinverters"
      },
      {
        "start": 363.217,
        "duration": 4.389,
        "time": "6:03",
        "text": "cost more, but they handle partial shading"
      },
      {
        "start": 367.696,
        "duration": 4.389,
        "time": "6:07",
        "text": "much better because every panel is tracked"
      },
      {
        "start": 372.174,
        "duration": 4.389,
        "time": "6:12",
        "text": "on its own. When your panels produce"
      },
      {
        "start": 376.652,
        "duration": 4.389,
        "time": "6:16",
        "text": "more power than the house uses, the"
      },
      {
        "start": 381.13,
        "duration": 4.389,
        "time": "6:21",
        "text": "inverter pushes the surplus onto the grid,"
      },
      {
        "start": 385.609,
        "duration": 4.389,
        "time": "6:25",
        "text": "and with net metering your utility credits"
      },
      {
        "start": 390.087,
        "duration": 4.389,
        "time": "6:30",
        "text": "you for it. For safety, a grid-tied"
      },
      {
        "start": 394.565,
        "duration": 4.389,
        "time": "6:34",
        "text": "inverter shuts down automatically during a power"
      },
      {
        "start": 399.043,
        "duration": 4.389,
        "time": "6:39",
        "text": "outage so it can't send current into"
      },
      {
        "start": 403.522,
        "duration": 4.389,
        "time": "6:43",
        "text": "lines that utility crews are repairing."
      },
      {
        "start": 408,
        "duration": 4.464,
        "time": "6:48",
        "text": "That shutdown is exactly why batteries have"
      },
      {
        "start": 412.556,
        "duration": 4.464,
        "time": "6:52",
        "text": "become so popular. A home battery stores"
      },
      {
        "start": 417.111,
        "duration": 4.464,
        "time": "6:57",
        "text": "surplus solar energy during the day so"
      },
      {
        "start": 421.667,
        "duration": 4.464,
        "time": "7:01",
        "text": "you can use it in the evening,"
      },
      {
        "start": 426.222,
        "duration": 4.464,
        "time": "7:06",
        "text": "when demand and electricity prices are highest."
      },
      {
        "start": 430.778,
        "duration": 4.464,
        "time": "7:10",
        "text": "Most home batteries today use lithium iron"
      },
      {
        "start": 435.333,
        "duration": 4.464,
        "time": "7:15",
        "text": "phosphate chemistry, which is safer and lasts"
      },
      {
        "start": 439.889,
        "duration": 4.464,
        "time": "7:19",
        "text": "longer than the lithium chemistry in older"
      },
      {
        "start": 444.444,
        "duration": 4.464,
        "time": "7:24",
        "text": "electric cars. A typical home battery stores"
      },
      {
        "start": 449,
        "duration": 4.464,
        "time": "7:29",
        "text": "between ten and fifteen kilowatt hours, enough"
      },
      {
        "start": 453.556,
        "duration": 4.464,
        "time": "7:33",
        "text": "to run the essentials through a night."
      },
      {
        "start": 458.111,
        "duration": 4.464,
        "time": "7:38",
        "text": "With a battery and the right inverter,"
      },
      {
        "start": 462.667,
        "duration": 4.464,
        "time": "7:42",
        "text": "your system can keep the lights on"
      },
      {
        "start": 467.222,
        "duration": 4.464,
        "time": "7:47",
        "text": "during a blackout by forming its own"
      },
      {
        "start": 471.778,
        "duration": 4.464,
        "time": "7:51",
        "text": "small island grid. Batteries add significant cost,"
      },
      {
        "start": 476.333,
        "duration": 4.464,
        "time": "7:56",
        "text": "though, so whether one makes sense depends"
      },
      {
        "start": 480.889,
        "duration": 4.464,
        "time": "8:00",
        "text": "on your utility's rates and how often"
      },
      {
        "start": 485.444,
        "duration": 4.464,
        "time": "8:05",
        "text": "the power goes out."
      },
      {
        "start": 490,
        "duration": 3.574,
        "time": "8:10",
        "text": "So, is solar worth it? For most"
      },
      {
        "start": 493.647,
        "duration": 3.574,
        "time": "8:13",
        "text": "homes with a sunny, unshaded roof, a"
      },
      {
        "start": 497.294,
        "duration": 3.574,
        "time": "8:17",
        "text": "solar system pays for itself in roughly"
      },
      {
        "start": 500.941,
        "duration": 3.574,
        "time": "8:20",
        "text": "six to ten years, and panels are"
      },
      {
        "start": 504.588,
        "duration": 3.574,
        "time": "8:24",
        "text": "usually warrantied for twenty five years. Panels"
      },
      {
        "start": 508.235,
        "duration": 3.574,
        "time": "8:28",
        "text": "slowly lose about half a percent of"
      },
      {
        "start": 511.882,
        "duration": 3.574,
        "time": "8:31",
        "text": "their output each year, so after twenty"
      },
      {
        "start": 515.529,
        "duration": 3.574,
        "time": "8:35",
        "text": "five years they still produce close to"
      },
      {
        "start": 519.176,
        "duration": 3.574,
        "time": "8:39",
        "text": "ninety percent of their original power. The"
      },
      {
        "start": 522.824,
        "duration": 3.574,
        "time": "8:42",
        "text": "key takeaway: a solar panel is just"
      },
      {
        "start": 526.471,
        "duration": 3.574,
        "time": "8:46",
        "text": "billions of photons knocking electrons loose in"
      },
      {
        "start": 530.118,
        "duration": 3.574,
        "time": "8:50",
        "text": "silicon, and everything else is about collecting,"
      },
      {
        "start": 533.765,
        "duration": 3.574,
        "time": "8:53",
        "text": "converting and storing that energy efficiently. If"
      },
      {
        "start": 537.412,
        "duration": 3.574,
        "time": "8:57",
        "text": "this helped, check out our follow-up video"
      },
      {
        "start": 541.059,
        "duration": 3.574,
        "time": "9:01",
        "text": "on sizing a system for your own"
      },
      {
        "start": 544.706,
        "duration": 3.574,
        "time": "9:04",
        "text": "home, and I'll see you in the"
      },
      {
        "start": 548.353,
        "duration": 3.574,
        "time": "9:08",
        "text": "next one."
      }
    ]
